    "descriptions": {
      "value": [
        {
          "resource_id": "levelled_description",
          "stats": {
            "id": "levelled_description_d4101b08e485",
            "level": {
              "value": 9
            },
            "description": {
              "value": "The fey influence on your form and features grows even more powerful and notable.\n\nYou gain one of the following features and abilities; this must be the same animal or fey type as you chose for Fey Influence.\n\n- **Anteater** You become an expert in primal DCs and spell attack rolls. You can cast slow as an innate primal spell once per day.\n- **Cat** Sith You laugh off the outraged curses of those you have tricked or wronged. Whenever a creature targets you with a misfortune effect, make a DC 13 flat check. On a success, you are unaffected.\n- **Cursed** Bluebird You have enough control over your curse to turn a bane into a minor blessing. Once per day, you can temporarily transform yourself or an ally into a blue bird, as a 4th-level pest form (bird only) targeting one willing creature.\n- **Dryad** Your hair becomes intermixed with delicate but razor-edged leaves that move as you command. You gain a leaves ranged unarmed attack that deals 1d6 slashing damage. Your leaves are in the dart weapon group and have the magical and unarmed traits.\n- **Faun** You can cast charm, sleep, and triple time as innate primal spells once per day each. Whenever you cast one of these spells, you can Step or Stride as part of the activity.\n- **Gremlin** You become an expert in primal DCs and spell attack rolls. You can cast mad monkeys (Advanced Player's Guide 222) as an innate primal spell once per day.\n- **Monarch** Once per day, you gain the ability to manifest a pair of exquisite butterfly wings. These wings remain for 10 minutes. You gain a fly Speed equal to your Speed while you've manifested your wings.\n- **Unicorn** You become trained in Medicine, or an expert if you were already trained. You gain a +2 status bonus to saves against poison and charm effects."
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
